We establish the optimal Lipschitz regularity of very weak solutions for the measure-valued elliptic problem \begin{equation*} 
\div D_u + \betah \in \partial_{\mathbf{v}} \phi (u) = \mu \quad \mbox{in} \ \Omega,
\end{equation*} with Dirichlet boundary conditions and $\mu$ an arbitrary measure. This extends prior research, such as Agostinelli-Birkar-Corti-Danilov-Robbiano's work on regular elliptic equations and ours with Vessella on parabolic problems.

